maru-prefix \22\22) base-name)))\0A                  `(define-C-function ,maru-name ,return-type ,foreign-name ,param-types)))\0A              entries))))\0A\0A(define-form define-C-variable (maru-name foreign-name type . attributes)\0A  (let ((fv (eval-in-host `(C-variable ,(symbol->string foreign-name)\0A                                       ',type ,@attributes))))\0A    `(define ,maru-name ,fv)))\0A\0A(define-form string->C-string (obj)\0A  ;; OPTIMIZATION: use the C-string compiler special form to emit cstrings when\0A  ;; literals are immediately passed to string->C-string. ideally it\0A  ;; should be done by some compiler macro like facility.\0A  (cond\0A    ((is <string> obj)\0A     `(C-string ,obj))\0A    ;; FIXME WTF is going on here? can't use (feature\0A    ;; emit-with-object-headers) directly, because it evaluates to\0A    ;; false. but how? only the slave env should have that variable\0A    ;; defined, and it's true while compiling eval.l\0A    ((eval '(feature emit-with-object-headers))\0A      `(%string->C-string ,obj))\0A    (else obj)))\0A\0A;; NOTE libc.l may choose to replace this with libc/strlen\0A(define-function C-string-length (cstr)\0A  (let ((i 0))\0A    (while (char-at cstr i)\0A      (incr i))\0A    i))\0A\00"
